nodecode-detox is a rewrite of kellycryptos's kellycryptos/hermes-detox:

https://github.com/kellycryptos/hermes-detox
commit 6efe12bea00546d0e200c67c7afec5e1ac056ce7
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 kellycryptos (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole plugin, in Common Lisp against the Nodecode cell contract. The
hook that turns an oversized tool result into a compact report is one hook on the
`:tool` point, which wraps a single tool dispatch where the original wrapped
Hermes's `transform_tool_result` and `transform_terminal_output`. The three
retrieval tools keep their names and their meanings (`detox_inspect`,
`detox_search`, `detox_status`), and `/detox status|inspect|search|purge` keeps its
four subcommands. The report keeps the original's shape: a header naming the tool
and the size kept, the extractor summary, the first and last few lines carrying
the original's own line numbers, every error and warning line with its number, and
how to ask for more. The line-number contract is the same, so a number read in a
report is a number the retrieval tools take. The settings are the original's,
with one change of units: `max_report_percent` is an integer where the original's
`max_ratio` was a float, because a section field is an integer or a string here.

Left out, and why: the SQLite evidence store became one text file and one
metadata file per record under the home - no native library, no WAL, and a record
the operator can read or delete with the tools they already have; concurrent
writers are served by a lock instead of a busy timeout. The original's six
content extractors (pytest/unittest/jest/cargo/go, gcc/clang/rustc/TypeScript,
terminal, JSON, file listings, plain text) became one light classifier naming the
shape (tests, build, listing, json, text) with a summary of a line or two each,
so a report says less about an unusual log than the original's did; the full text
is kept, so nothing is lost, only summarised less deeply. Hermes's own redaction
helpers became this cell's pattern list, with the same honest limit: a pattern
cannot catch every secret. The `post_compaction` relink of records between
session ids, the retention throttle and the six-hourly prune timer are gone: this
cell prunes at start and on `/detox purge`, and scopes a search to the running
session through its metadata instead of relinking anything. The Hermes slash
command's dialog, the benchmark runner, the demo, and the stage reports are not
carried over.
